  "body": "Currently we do not increment the per-host backoff counter on 405 (method not allowed) responses. If we get a 405, it suggests a poorly-configured destination, so we should back off.\n\nIndeed, the only 40x codes we do back off for are 401, 429, and (sometimes) 404. If our spec actually properly defined the valid error responses, we could do much better here.",
